/*
Detection Rule: AWS S3 High-Volume GetObject Data Exfiltration
Author: Bryan Jorge
MITRE ATT&CK: T1530 - Data from Cloud Storage
Severity: High
Description: Detects bulk S3 GetObject activity that may indicate data
exfiltration. Attackers with valid credentials will often enumerate and
download large volumes of objects in a short window. This rule flags
principals exceeding download count or volume thresholds, and increases
severity when data flows to external IP addresses. Requires S3 data
event logging enabled in CloudTrail (not enabled by default).
*/

index=aws_cloudtrail sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail"
    eventSource="s3.amazonaws.com"
    eventName="GetObject"
    errorCode=""

| eval actor=coalesce(userIdentity.userName, userIdentity.principalId)
| eval bucket_name=requestParameters.bucketName
| eval object_key=requestParameters.key
| eval bytes_out=coalesce(additionalEventData.bytesTransferredOut, 0)

| eval ip_class=case(
    match(sourceIPAddress, "^10\.|^172\.(1[6-9]|2\d|3[01])\.|^192\.168\."), "internal",
    match(sourceIPAddress, "amazonaws\.com"),                                 "aws_service",
    1==1,                                                                     "external")

/* Aggregate per actor per 15-minute window */
| bin _time span=15m
| stats
    count                    AS get_count,
    dc(bucket_name)          AS distinct_buckets,
    dc(object_key)           AS distinct_objects,
    sum(bytes_out)           AS total_bytes,
    values(bucket_name)      AS buckets_accessed,
    values(sourceIPAddress)  AS source_ips,
    values(ip_class)         AS ip_classes,
    min(_time)               AS first_seen,
    max(_time)               AS last_seen
    by actor, _time

| eval total_mb=round(total_bytes / 1048576, 2)

| where get_count > 500
    OR distinct_buckets > 5
    OR (total_mb > 1000 AND match(ip_classes, "external"))
    OR (get_count > 100 AND match(ip_classes, "external"))

/* Score based on volume, destination, and bucket spread */
| eval risk_score=0
| eval risk_score=if(total_mb > 5000 AND match(ip_classes,"external"),   risk_score+60, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(get_count > 1000 AND match(ip_classes,"external"),  risk_score+50, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(total_mb > 1000 AND match(ip_classes,"external"),   risk_score+40, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(distinct_buckets > 10,                              risk_score+25, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(get_count > 500,                                    risk_score+15, risk_score)
| eval risk_score=if(match(ip_classes,"external"),                       risk_score+10, risk_score)

| eval alert_title="S3 Data Exfiltration Suspected: " . actor
| table _time, alert_title, actor, get_count, distinct_buckets,
        distinct_objects, total_mb, buckets_accessed,
        source_ips, ip_classes, risk_score, first_seen, last_seen
| sort -risk_score

/*
TUNING PARAMETERS:
- get_count threshold: Run in search mode for 2 weeks first; set threshold at
  mean + 2 standard deviations for your environment's baseline
- total_mb threshold: Adjust based on typical ETL workload volumes
- ip_class filter: Add | where match(ip_classes,"external") to alert only on
  external destinations (eliminates most ETL pipeline false positives)
- Whitelist examples:
  | where NOT match(actor, "ETLRole|BackupRole|DataSync|GlueRole|SageMakerRole")
  | where NOT match(buckets_accessed, "public-assets|static-website|open-data")

FALSE POSITIVES:
- ETL pipelines performing bulk reads for analytics or machine learning workloads
- Cross-region S3 replication jobs triggered by policy changes
- AWS Backup, DataSync, or third-party backup tools reading large object sets
- Batch processing jobs (AWS Batch, Glue) reading full dataset partitions

RECOMMENDED RESPONSE:
1. Identify the actor type — is this a human user, service role, or pipeline?
2. Cross-reference source IPs against known corporate, vendor, and cloud runner IPs
3. Assess the data classification of the buckets accessed (PII, financial, IP)
4. If malicious: disable the actor's IAM credentials and apply explicit S3 deny policy
5. Apply S3 Block Public Access and restrict GetObject to specific VPC endpoints
6. Notify data governance team if sensitive data volumes were transferred externally

INVESTIGATION QUERIES:
- List all objects downloaded: index=aws_cloudtrail sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail"
  eventName="GetObject" userIdentity.userName=<actor> earliest=<first_seen>
  | stats count by requestParameters.bucketName, requestParameters.key
- Confirm external egress: index=aws_cloudtrail sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail"
  eventName="GetObject" userIdentity.userName=<actor>
  | eval country=geoip(sourceIPAddress,"country") | stats count by country, sourceIPAddress
- Post-access IAM activity: index=aws_cloudtrail sourcetype="aws:cloudtrail"
  userIdentity.userName=<actor> eventSource="iam.amazonaws.com"
  | table _time, eventName, requestParameters

DATA SOURCES REQUIRED:
- AWS CloudTrail with S3 data events enabled (NOT enabled by default)
  Enable via: CloudTrail > Trail > Data Events > S3 > Log all events

HIGH-RISK INDICATORS:
- Source IP resolves to a residential ISP, VPN provider, or Tor exit node
- Actor's credentials were recently used from a new geolocation (correlate with
  access_key_new_geolocation rule)
- Downloads follow an enumeration pattern: ListBuckets → ListObjects → GetObject

PREVENTION MEASURES:
- Restrict S3 access via VPC endpoint policies to block external egress
- Enable S3 Block Public Access at the account level
- Enable Amazon Macie for automatic sensitive data discovery and alerting
- Apply SCP to restrict s3:GetObject to approved VPC endpoints organization-wide

RELATED TECHNIQUES:
- T1619 - Cloud Storage Object Discovery
- T1078.004 - Valid Accounts: Cloud Accounts
- T1537 - Transfer Data to Cloud Account

CHANGELOG:
v1.0 (2026-02-17): Initial release
*/
